PHASE 5 – PROJECT DEVELOPMENT

1. Introduction

Project development is the stage where the planned design and requirements are converted into an actual working application. FitBuddy is developed as a web-based fitness plan generator using HTML, CSS, and JavaScript.

2. Frontend Development

HTML is used to create the structure of the FitBuddy application. The webpage contains sections such as Home, Features, Fitness Plan Generator, About, and Footer.

The HTML structure provides the elements required for users to interact with the application.

3. Styling Development

CSS is used to improve the appearance of the application. It is used for page layout, typography, buttons, cards, forms, spacing, backgrounds, and responsive design.

The application is designed to provide a clean and simple user experience.

4. JavaScript Development

JavaScript provides the interactive functionality of FitBuddy.

When the user selects a fitness goal, fitness level, and number of workout days, JavaScript reads the selected values and generates an appropriate recommendation.

5. Fitness Goal Implementation

The application supports different fitness goals such as:

- Weight Loss
- Muscle Gain
- General Fitness
- Strength

Each goal has a different set of recommended exercises.

6. User Interaction

The user interacts with the application through dropdown menus and buttons. After selecting the required information, the user clicks the "Generate My Plan" button.

The application then displays the generated fitness recommendation.

7. Project Files

The main project files are:

FitBuddy/
│
├── index.html
├── style.css
├── script.js
└── README.md

"index.html" contains the webpage structure.

"style.css" contains the visual design and responsive styling.

"script.js" contains the interactive fitness plan generation functionality.

"README.md" contains information about the project.

8. Deployment

After development, the project files can be uploaded to a public GitHub repository. The repository provides a centralized location for storing and sharing the project files.

The project can also be deployed as a web application using a suitable hosting platform.

9. Development Outcome

At the end of the development stage, FitBuddy provides a functional interface where users can select their fitness preferences and generate a basic personalized workout recommendation.
